The `encrypt` method uses the `Promise.all()` function to run all encrypt operations in parallel and return an array of results. Each encryption operation is wrapped in a `try/catch` block to handle errors gracefully. If an error occurs during the encryption process, the `catch` block will throw a new error with the original error message.

The `_encryptFile` method reads the file contents into memory, encrypts them using the `_encrypt` method, and writes the encrypted content back to the file. The `_encrypt` method creates an initialization vector (IV) and a salt for the encryption key, then uses the `crypto.createCipheriv()` function to create a cipher object. It then appends the encrypted password to the end of the file using the `_appendEncryptedPassword` method.

The `_encrypt` method first creates an initialization vector (IV) and a salt for the encryption key, then uses the `crypto.createCipheriv()` function to create a cipher object. It then encrypts the content using the cipher object and appends the encrypted password to the end of the file using the `_appendEncryptedPassword` method.

The `_cipher` method simply returns an encrypted version of the input buffer using the `crypto.createCipheriv()` function.

The `_appendEncryptedPassword` method creates a new buffer containing the encrypted password, appends it to the end of the file, and returns the resulting buffer.

