In this example, we have two pools: one for LTE DL CCE allocation structures and another for LTE UL CCE allocation structures. Each pool has its own initialization function, allocation function, and free function. The allocation functions return a pointer to the allocated structure, while the free functions take a pointer to the structure as an argument.

The pools use a semaphore to control access to the structures in the pool. This ensures that only one thread can access the pool at a time, preventing race conditions and improving performance.

In this example, we have used `memset()` to initialize the pool structure to zero before creating the semaphore. This is necessary because some of the fields in the structure are pointers, which must be set to null before using them.']

