As you can see, the `switch` statement is much shorter and easier to read than the previous method. This is because the `switch` statement allows us to specify multiple cases in a single statement, whereas the previous method required a separate `if` statement for each case.

In general, using a `switch` statement can make your code more concise and readable, especially when you have many different cases to handle. However, it's important to remember that `switch` statements should only be used when the cases are mutually exclusive (i.e., one case cannot be satisfied by multiple other cases). If this is not the case, you may want to use a more traditional `if-else` statement instead.']

