['```cpp
#include <cstdint>
#include <random>
#include <mutex>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <vector>

namespace FinancialRNG {
    class MTGenerator {
    public:
        MTGenerator(const uint64_t seed) : mt19937_(seed), uniform_dist_(0, std::numeric_limits<uint64_t>::max()) {}

        uint64_t getRandomNumber() {
            return uniform_dist_(mt19937_);
        }

    private:
        std::mt19937 mt19937_;
        std::uniform_int_distribution<uint64_t> uniform_dist_;
    };

    uint64_t generateSeed() {
        // Generate a cryptographically secure seed using a random source
        std::random_device rd;
        return rd();
    }

    static std::mutex mtx;
    static std::unordered_map<uint64_t, MTGenerator> generators;

    uint64_t getRandomNumber(const uint64_t seed) {
        // Lock the mutex to prevent concurrent access to the generator map
        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mtx);

        // Check if a generator for the given seed already exists
        auto it = generators.find(seed);
        if (it != generators.end()) {
            return it->second.getRandomNumber();
        }

        // If not, create a new generator and insert it into the map
        MTGenerator generator(seed);
        generators.insert({seed, generator});
        return generator.getRandomNumber();
    }
}
```
The above code defines a `FinancialRNG::MTGenerator` class that generates random numbers using the Mersenne Twister (Mersenne Twister) algorithm. The constructor takes a seed as an argument and initializes an instance of `std::mt19937` with it. The `getRandomNumber()` method returns a uniformly distributed 64-bit integer using an instance of `std::uniform_int_distribution`.

The `generateSeed()` function generates a cryptographically secure seed using a random source, which is used to initialize the `MTGenerator` instances. The `getRandomNumber(const uint64_t seed)` function takes a seed as input and returns a uniformly distributed random number using the corresponding `MTGenerator` instance. If no `MTGenerator` instance exists for the given seed, it creates a new one and inserts it into the map of generators.

The `mtx` mutex is used to prevent concurrent access to the generator map, ensuring that only one thread can modify the map at a time. The `generators` map stores the `MTGenerator` instances with their corresponding seeds as keys. The function returns the random number generated by the corresponding `MTGenerator` instance for the given seed.

This implementation provides low-latency order execution and high concurrency by leveraging the Mersenne Twister algorithm, which is considered to be a fast and highly uniform PRNG. The use of a mutex ensures thread safety, while the map of generators allows for efficient access and creation of new instances as needed under high concurrency conditions.']

