Here is a suggested design for the modular C++ library that dynamically manages a connection pool for a high-throughput, distributed transaction processing environment:

1. Connection Pool Management
--------------

The connection pool will be responsible for managing connections to external systems and services. It will use a thread-safe data structure to store connections and provide access to them in a synchronized manner. The pool will also manage the lifetime of connections, closing them when they are no longer needed or after a certain time has passed.
```cpp
class ConnectionPool {
  private:
    std::unordered_map<std::string, std::shared_ptr<Connection>> connections_;
    std::mutex mutex_;

  public:
    void add(const std::string& id, const std::shared_ptr<Connection>& connection) {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
      connections_.insert({id, connection});
    }

    void remove(const std::string& id) {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
      connections_.erase(id);
    }

    std::shared_ptr<Connection> get(const std::string& id) {
      std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
      auto it = connections_.find(id);
      if (it != connections_.end()) {
        return it->second;
      }
      return nullptr;
    }
}
