The `processEvent()` method is responsible for processing an event received from Kafka using Apache Flink. It creates a DataFrame object using the `flink::createDataFrame()` method, adds columns with the key and value of the incoming event, groups the data by the key, and applies a count aggregation on the "value" column. Finally, it writes the resulting DataFrame to HDFS using an HDFSWriter object created from the HDFSClient.

