The `BatchDataProcessor` struct also includes a backpressure mechanism to manage data flow effectively, preventing data overflow in the system. The struct is designed to scale both vertically to handle increased data volumes and horizontally to manage extreme data spikes, considering the trade-offs between resource utilization and operational complexity.

The `BatchDataProcessor` struct also includes a performance monitoring tool to track data processing times, memory usage, and data transfer latencies. The struct uses this data to dynamically adjust job parameters, such as batch sizes, thread counts, and retry intervals, to optimize performance under varying data loads. The struct also implements strategies to detect and recover from performance bottlenecks, ensuring continuous data processing even in the face of transient errors.

The `BatchDataProcessor` struct also includes an error handling system that differentiates between transient and permanent data processing failures. The struct uses a resilient logging system that records detailed metadata, including data type, size, processing time, and error context, to facilitate post-mortem analysis. The struct also implements a notification system to alert stakeholders of critical failures and provide recovery recommendations. Finally, the struct ensures logs are encrypted and stored securely for compliance and auditing purposes, while evaluating the balance between storing extensive logs and using more compact summaries to optimize storage efficiency.']

