The `MTGenerator` class encapsulates all functionality within the `FinancialRNG` namespace. It has a constructor that accepts a unique seed, which is used to initialize an instance of the `std::mt19937` engine. Each instance of the `MTGenerator` class maintains its own random number stream, and the seeds are stored in a static map to ensure no two instances share the same seed unless explicitly requested.

The `getRandomNumber()` method returns a uniformly distributed 64-bit integer using the `std::uniform_int_distribution<uint64_t>` class from the C++ standard library. The `std::mt19937` engine is used for number generation, and the random seed is generated using the `generateSeed()` method.

