To improve performance and scalability, this service uses Redis or Memcached for session management and token validation, with appropriate cache invalidation policies to avoid stale data issues. It also includes rate-limiting and throttling mechanisms to prevent abuse and ensure fair usage of the authentication service.

The service is designed to handle a large number of concurrent requests without performance degradation, with load balancing and auto-scaling policies for handling varying loads and optimizing resource allocation based on real-time metrics. It also includes comprehensive error handling and retry mechanisms for network failures and service unavailability, as well as detailed error messages and logging for debugging and auditing purposes.

