The class is designed with thread safety and scalability in mind, supporting concurrent read and write operations across multiple threads and processes. It also includes fine-grained locking mechanisms to prevent deadlocks and ensure deadlock-free synchronization. Additionally, it includes monitoring resource usage and throttling to detect and mitigate hotspots, ensuring fair access to shared resources.

The system is adaptable to future changes, supporting easy integration with new services and features. It also considers operational constraints such as limited memory and CPU resources and makes trade-offs between efficiency, usability, maintainability, and scalability.

