This code defines a `MetricManager` class that manages a dynamic set of `MetricData` objects. The class provides methods to add, remove and get the value of metrics. The implementation uses a map to store the metric names and values, with a mutex and condition variable for synchronizing access to the map.

In the `main()` function, an instance of the `MetricManager` class is created and some metrics are added and removed using the methods provided by the class. The value of a metric can be retrieved using the `getValue()` method.

This code demonstrates how a scalable, modular, and fault-tolerant C++ library module can be implemented to manage a dynamic set of `MetricData` objects for processing high-velocity streaming metrics in a distributed analytics platform. It includes seamless integration with external data sources, performance optimization techniques, error handling mechanisms, scalability and concurrency features, resource management strategies, and testing and validation capabilities.']

