Here is an example implementation of the `generateMD5Hash` function in C#:
```
using System;
using System.Security.Cryptography;

public static string GenerateMD5Hash(string input) {
    using (var md5 = MD5.Create()) {
        byte[] hash = md5.ComputeHash(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(input));
        return BitConverter.ToString(hash).Replace("-", "").ToLower();
    }
}
```
This function takes a string input and returns its MD5 hash using the `MD5` class in the `System.Security.Cryptography` namespace. The `using` statement ensures that the instance of the `MD5` class is disposed properly after use. The `ComputeHash` method computes the MD5 hash of the input string and returns it as a byte array. The `BitConverter` class is used to convert the byte array into a hexadecimal string, which is returned by the function.

Here is an example implementation of the `mergeResourceBundles` function in C#:
```
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.Linq;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration;
using Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Options;

public static Task<ResourceStore> MergeResourceBundlesAsync(List<string> resourceBundlePaths, CancellationToken cancellationToken = default) {
    var serviceCollection = new ServiceCollection();
    serviceCollection.AddTransient<IFileReader, FileReader>();
    serviceCollection.AddTransient<ICustomCompressionProvider, CustomCompressionProvider>();
    serviceCollection.AddSingleton<ResourceStore>();

    var services = serviceCollection.BuildServiceProvider();
    var resourceStore = services.GetRequiredService<ResourceStore>();

    foreach (var resourceBundlePath in resourceBundlePaths) {
        var fileReader = services.GetRequiredService<IFileReader>();
        var compressionProvider = services.GetRequiredService<ICustomCompressionProvider>();

        using (var stream = fileReader.OpenRead(resourceBundlePath)) {
            if (stream == null) {
                throw new FileNotFoundException($"Resource bundle not found at path '{resourceBundlePath}'.");
            }

            var extension = Path.GetExtension(resourceBundlePath);
            var compressionType = extension.ToLower().EndsWith("gz") ? CompressionType.GZip : CompressionType.None;

            using (var compressedStream = compressionProvider.Compress(stream, compressionType)) {
                using (var reader = new StreamReader(compressedStream)) {
                    var resourceBundle = ResourceBundle.FromJson(reader);
                    resourceStore.AddResourceBundle(resourceBundle);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return Task.FromResult(resourceStore);
}
```
This function takes a list of paths to resource bundles and merges them into a unified, optimized resource store. The `ServiceCollection` class is used to configure the service provider with dependencies on the `IFileReader`, `ICustomCompressionProvider`, and `ResourceStore` classes. The `BuildServiceProvider` method creates an instance of the service provider that can be used to resolve services and resources.

The function then loops over each resource bundle path in the list, uses the `GetRequiredService` method to resolve an instance of the `IFileReader` and `ICustomCompressionProvider` services, and then uses those instances to read and compress the file stream for each resource bundle. Finally, it creates a `ResourceStore` instance and adds each resource bundle to it using the `AddResourceBundle` method.

The function returns a task that completes when the resource store has been populated with all of the resource bundles in the list. The returned task will have a `ResourceStore` object as its result, which can be used to query and manage the merged resource store.']

